592-4eee-b204-502a805fbc8c","oracle_text":"This land enters tapped.\n{T}: Add {G}.\n{1}{G}: This land becomes a 3/3 green Ape creature with trample until end of turn. It's still a land. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["G"],"released_at":"2018-04-06","toughness":null,"type_line":"Land"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you don't have a commander, Command Tower's ability produces no mana.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have two commanders, the ability adds one mana of any color in their combined color identities.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If your commander is a card that has no colors in its color identity, Command Tower's ability produces no mana. It doesn't produce {C}.","oracle_id":"0895c9b7-ae7d-4bb3-af17-3b75deb50a25","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Settle the Wreckage targets only the player. Creatures with hexproof that player controls will be exiled as this spell resolves.","oracle_id":"2a2ea189-b663-4f4a-bb23-ff7a4af25f71","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"That player can find fewer basic land cards than the number of exiled creatures, whether because they want to or because they don’t have that many basic land cards left.","oracle_id":"2a2ea189-b663-4f4a-bb23-ff7a4af25f71","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The number of lands that player may find is the number of attacking creatures that were exiled, even if some of those creatures were tokens, weren’t creature cards, or didn’t end up in exile (most likely because one was that player’s commander in the Commander variant).","oracle_id":"2a2ea189-b663-4f4a-bb23-ff7a4af25f71","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature.","oracle_id":"b53f216d-1592-4eee-b204-502a805fbc8c","published_at":"2008-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Activating the ability that turns it into a creature while it's already a creature will override any effects that set its power and/or toughness to a specific number. However, any effect that raises or lowers power and/or toughness (such as the effect created by Giant Growth, Glorious Anthem, or a +1/+1 counter) will continue to apply.","oracle_id":"b53f216d-1592-4eee-b204-502a805fbc8c","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
